51d","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Exception-not-ActualOwnerAcceptance","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/normative_statement","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.constraint-cycle-safety-invariant","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/constraint-cycle-safety-invariant/v1/definition.json","sha256":"bf829b78c06764c34db536edd838cce4683716935ca0ec5bd9742f8d66e573fb","version_ref":"cal.definition.constraint-cycle-safety-invariant@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character":0},{"actual_outcome_target_in_T":false,"clause_id":"CCS-015","end_character":897,"excerpt":"\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nA value-cycle edge guard is the CyberAlchemy v2 invariant that no relation,\nedge type, or ontology movement may simultaneously:\n\n- constrain the value, label, authority state, schema field, or validation\n  outcome of another artifact; and\n- be allowed to participate in a cycle without an explicit acyclicity\n  constraint.\n\nIf a proposed relation needs both properties, it must stop at schema governance\nand receive a contextuality-obstruction review before it can influence\nauthority, ontology, validation, or implementation.","excerpt_sha256":"a4a643ec9e181b236682ada36be415c3848ad3b5127d439192b3d9f0b4d5204e","necessary_declaration_guard_in_T":true,"query_id":"Instance-not-ActualSourceFidelity","selected_in_T":false,"selector":"/voices/scientific_formal/normative_statement","source":{"definition_id":"cal.definition.constraint-cycle-safety-invariant","path":"evidence/migrations/cyberalchemy-v2-to-lab/candidates/0004-artifact-reconstruction-pipeline/layers/l1-semantic-repeatability/definitions/constraint-cycle-safety-invariant/v1/definition.json","sha256":"bf829b78c06764c34db536edd838cce4683716935ca0ec5bd9742f8d66e573fb","version_ref":"cal.definition.constraint-cycle-safety-invariant@1.0.0-candidate.1"},"start_character"